  "problem": "Let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T$ and ${u}_{1},{u}_{2}\\in {R}^{3}.$  Consider the following statement:\n\n*If ${u}_{1}-{u}_{2}\\ne 0$ and $T({u}_{1})-T({u}_{2})=0,$ then $\\text{__________}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$\n- $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 3$\n- $T$ is invertible",
